## Phase 2 — Dispatcher Dashboard

**The most feature-rich role — main operational interface.**

### 2.1 — Live Map (upgrade existing)
Keep the Leaflet map but add:
- Emergency markers (red pin) showing location + priority badge (HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW)
- Ambulance markers colored by status: green=AVAILABLE, yellow=ASSIGNED, red=ON_ROUTE
- Click ambulance → popup shows: ID, status, current speed, active emergency ID
- Click emergency marker → popup shows: ID, priority, status, assigned ambulance

### 2.2 — Create Emergency Panel
Form with:
- Click-on-map to pick coordinates (instead of typing lat/lon)
- Priority selector (HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW)
- Submit → `POST /api/emergencies` with JWT
- On success: new emergency marker appears on map instantly
- Show toast: "Emergency EMG-XXX created — dispatching..."

### 2.3 — Emergency Queue Panel
Real-time list of all active emergencies pulled from `GET /api/emergencies/status/PENDING` and `GET /api/emergencies/status/ASSIGNED`:
- Sorted by priority (HIGH first)
- Each row shows: ID, priority badge, status, time since creation, assigned ambulance (or "Pending")
- Color-coded rows: red=HIGH, orange=MEDIUM, blue=LOW

### 2.4 — Fleet Status Panel
From `GET /api/ambulances/available` and `GET /api/ambulances/fleet`:
- Summary counts: X Available / Y Assigned / Z On Route
- Per-ambulance row: ID, status pill, current speed if moving

